alse,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.5,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"scrofula","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.95,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"sexual_function","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":2.79,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"spleen_disease","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":1,"lift":2.17,"evidence_tier":"sparse"},{"concept_id":"syphilis","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.94,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:116-eringo-or-sea-holly":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Eringo, Or Sea-Holly","headword":"Eringo, Or Sea-Holly","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"The plant is venereal, and breeds seed exceedingly, and strengthens the spirit procreative; it is hot and moist, and under the celestial Balance. The decoction of the root hereof in wine, is very effectual to open obstructions of the spleen and liver, and helps yellow jaundice, dropsy, pains of the loins, and wind cholic, provokes urine, and expels the stone, procures women’s courses. The continued use of the decoction for fifteen days, taken fasting, and next to bedward, doth help the stranguary, the difficulty and stoppage of urine, and the stone, as well as all defects of the reins and kidneys; and if the said drink be continued longer, it is said that it cures the stone; it is found good against the French pox. The roots bruised and applied outwardly, help the kernels of the throat, commonly called the king’s evil; or taking inwardly, and applied to the place stung or bitten by any serpent, heal it speedily. If the roots be bruised, and boiled in old hog’s grease, or salted lard, and broken bones, thorns &c. remaining in the flesh, they do not only draw them forth, but heal up the place again, gathering new flesh where it was consumed. The juice of the leaves dropped into the ear, helps imposthumes therein. The distilled water of the whole herb, when the leaves and stalks are young, is profitable drank for all the purposes aforesaid; and helps the melancholy of the heart, and is available in quartan and quotidian agues; as also for them that have their necks drawn awry, and cannot turn them without turning their whole body.","spans":[{"start":27,"end":38,"concept_id":"sexual_function","polarity":"action"},{"start":234,"end":240,"concept_id":"spleen_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":269,"end":277,"concept_id":"jaundice","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":279,"end":285,"concept_id":"edema_dropsy","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":316,"end":322,"concept_id":"colic","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":324,"end":338,"concept_id":"diuresis","polarity":"action"},{"start":355,"end":360,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":362,"end":386,"concept_id":"amenorrhea","polarity":"action"},{"start":491,"end":501,"concept_id":"dysuria","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":522,"end":539,"concept_id":"diuresis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":549,"end":554,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":586,"end":591,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":596,"end":603,"concept_id":"kidney_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":677,"end":682,"concept_id":"urolithiasis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":720,"end":723,"concept_id":"syphilis","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":775,"end":796,"concept_id":"scrofula","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":818,"end":829,"concept_id":"scrofula","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":876,"end":881,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":885,"end":891,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":899,"end":906,"concept_id":"envenomation","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1190,"end":1221,"concept_id":"ear_disease","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1374,"end":1397,"concept_id":"melancholy","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1419,"end":1426,"concept_id":"malaria","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1431,"end":1440,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1441,"end":1446,"concept_id":"fever","polarity":"therapeutic"},{"start":1481,"end":1497,"concept_id":"convulsions","polarity":"therapeutic"}]}},"gloss":{"cul:116-eringo-or-sea-holly":{"27":"increases sperm / breeds seed","234":"spleen: hardness, swelling, stoppings of the spleen","269":"yellow jaundice, black jaundice","279":"dropsy, dropsies","316":"cholic: colic, griping abdominal pain","324":"provokes urine: diuretic","355":"the stone (urinary calculus)","362":"provokes / brings down the terms, courses: emmenagogue","491":"strangury (stranguary): slow, painful urination","522":"stopping / stoppage of urine: urinary retention","549":"the stone (urinary calculus)","586":"reins: kidneys","596":"kidneys","677":"the stone (urinary calculus)","720":"the (French) pox: syphilis","775":"kernels in / of the throat, neck or ears: swollen glands","818":"king's evil: scrofula","876":"bitten or stung","885":"bitten or stung","899":"serpents, vipers, adders, scorpions, wasps","1190":"dropped into the ears, eases the pains / kills the worms","1374":"melancholy diseases, melancholy dreams","1419":"quartan ague (fever every fourth day)","1431":"quotidian ague (daily fever)","1441":"agues: intermittent fevers","1481":"stiff sinews"}},"images":[]}